<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">2.In Sept 2018, the BOD of the Company decided to dispose off the forging business in the UK, pertaining to the company Stokes Group Limited. Due to that decision, the Group has discontinued the operations of SGL, classifying them as a disposal group, and reclassifying the P&amp;L AC of the Company to results from discontinued operations in its consolidated result. SGL got liquidated on 5.9.2023. The consolidated results include total income and PBT of INR 34.66 Mio pertaining to this discontinued operations for year ended 13.12.2023. For other comparable periods, the results of Stokes Group Ltd is nil. 3.In BM held on 14.12.22, took note of the proposal approved by CIE Galfor, S.A.U. (Galfor) to launch an active program to locate a buyer for the German Forging Operations comprising of CIE Forgings Germany GmbH (CFG) and its subsidiaries. In accordance with the applicable AS, considering Galfor’s decision to launch the program, all the German Forging Operation’s “assets and liabilities” were categorised as assets and liabilities held for sale and classified as discontinued operation. Further, the BOD of the HC at its meeting held on 10.8.23, approved the transaction of sale of 100% stake held by CFG in its subsidiaries in Germany namely Jeco Jellinghaus GmbH (JECO), Gesenkschmiede Schneider GmbH (GSA), Falkenroth Umformtechnik GmbH (FUG) and Schoneweiss &amp; Co. GmbH (SCG) to Mutares SE &amp; Co KgaA (the Buyer) (the Transaction). Thereafter, CFG as seller of JECO, GSA, FUG and SCG and the Buyer entered into binding agreements to give effect to the Transaction on 10.8.23. As per this agreement, under the relevant accounting standards effective 1.7.23, JECO, GSA, FUG and SCG results were not included in the consolidated results. The Foreign currency translation reserve (FCTR) (under other equity) pertaining to the disposed group amounting to INR 2,090.62 million (including INR 3,132 million in relation to translation of goodwill) is credited to Statement of Profit and Loss, during the year ended 13.12.23. FCTR is created by translation of disposal group results and financial position from foreign currency to INR as per applicable INDAS and is accumulated in FCTR until actual disposal. 4.The Group had recognised further loss on fair valuation of disposal group of INR 1,536.45 mio during FY13.12.23. Particulars31.3.24 (unaudited) 31.12.23(refer note 7)31.3.23(unaudited)31.12.23 (Audited) (Rs in million) I. Total income 7.67,Nil,5575.20,13909.34, II. Total Expenses 3.61,81.12,4835.55,8603.47 III. Profit/(loss) before tax (I-II) 4.06,(81.12),739.65,5305.87, IV. Loss on fair valuation of assets and liabilities of disposal group– Nil, Nil, Nil, (1536.45), V. Tax expense 1.26, Nil, 151.10,528.89, VI. Profit/(loss) from discontinued operations (III+IV-V) 2.80,(81.12),588.55,3240.53 8.CIE Aluminium Castings India Limited (CACIL) (formerly known as Aurangabad Electricals Limited), the company’s subsidiary is eligible for Government Grant income under Maharashtra Government Package Scheme of Incentives (PSI) 2013. This incentive is in the form of refund from the Government of Maharashtra on actual VAT/SGST paid by the company from the period 1.2.16 to 31.1.23 (7 years) with a maximum limit of INR2,674 Million. During the quarter, CACIL has received a period enhancement for this subsidy upto 31.1.25 and a maximum value enhancement upto INR3,112 Million. As a result of this extension, additional grant income of INR220 Million which pertains to the period upto 31.12.23, has been recognised in the Profit and Loss Account during the current quarter ended 31.3.24. 9.CIE Hosur Limited (CHL), a WOS of the Company  has entered into Share Subscription and Shareholders Agreement (SSSHA) with Ojaha Renewables Private Limited (ORPL) on 29.1.24 and as per SSSHA agreement, CHL will hold 27.89 % of Equity of ORPL. ORPL has allotted the equivalent equity share capital to CHL on 25.4.24 after the payment of share application money.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
